## Session 21 summary

**Corruption blocker CLOSED.** The intermittent iflush bad-magic / error-117 corruption (the open blocker from session 20) is fixed: `mxfs_dlm_reload_inode` was unconditionally staling inode cluster buffers that carried attached log items (`P20-CLUSTER-INVAL site=reload li_empty=0` observed pre-fix). Added the sess91-class `mxfs_buf_has_uncheckpointed_mods` guard (`P91-RELOAD-PROTECT`, fires ~30×/cycle). `scripts/repro_peer_find.sh`: **12/12 cycles clean** (prior ~50% fail rate), re-confirmed 4/4 on the final build.

**single_node_paired: FAIL 180% → PASS 102%.** Three instrumented root causes, each fixed and measured separately:
1. **Large folios silently disabled** — the 6.8 compat shim for `mapping_set_folio_min_order` (`xfs/xfs_platform.h`) was a no-op; now calls `mapping_set_large_folios()`. Data path went from 3254 singleton 4KB bios / 1722ms to clean 512KB stream / 834ms (native parity).
2. **Log slice too small** — `mkfs_mxfs` min bumped 32MB→64MB per node slice; the 1500-sync-log-write CIL storm dropped to native level (113 vs 107).
3. **P74 probe = hidden FUA read per extent allocation** — `b_mxfs_ag_gen` is never stamped, so the "rare" stale branch fired on every alloc (9248 SCSI READ_16 per rsync). Gated behind `mxfs.instr` (`xfs/libxfs/xfs_alloc.c`).

Side benefit: 2-node solo rsync 6.2s → ~3.7s. Current build `3B57EA84` deployed on test1/test2.

**Also done:** posix_semantics results-key split (`posix_semantics_single` PASS recorded / `posix_semantics_multi16` pending) across `posix_semantics.sh`, `SUCCESS_CRITERIA.md`, and `showstat.sh` — the dashboard now shows two differentiated rows (addresses your showstat complaint); stale combined key removed from `.criteria_results.json`. Memory written: `sess21-ccloop-perf-roots-and-reload-guard`. Diag scripts in tree: `diag_single_paired_phases.sh`, `diag_data_io_shape.sh`, `diag_rsync_io_shape.sh`.

**Open: scaling_curve FAIL (283% vs ≤150%).** Shape is a fixed multi-node penalty (flat ~7-10s from 2→16 nodes vs 3.3s solo), not super-linear contention. Instrumented root: CAW slot I/O on the create path — per file ≈2.5 serialized FUA READ_16 probes + CAW (`find_slot_skip` reads one 512B slot per round trip; `caw_count_resource_slots` on lock; `mxfs_dlm_caw_held` verify probes ~8079/run via P108/P106 checks), plus `bast_poll_fn` reading up to 256 held slots individually every 200ms (O(held) background IOPS; also only ever polls the FIRST 256 held slots — latent coverage gap). Promising next steps: cache the claimed slot index in the held-lock handle so held-checks/unlock skip the hash probe (1 read instead of chain walk), batch linear-probe reads (8-16 slots per READ_16), and bound/rotate the poller batch.

**Remaining for the gate:** fix scaling_curve, run `posix_semantics_multi16`, then full `verify_ship.sh` end-to-end. Criteria marker **not** written — gate not green.

